# WinDoesNot portable desktop sources – @VERSION@

This is a source export for experienced Arch/CachyOS users, not an operating
system image or a prebuilt desktop. For the supported starting point, use the
live ISO at https://windoesnot.me/download/.

Requirements
------------
Arch/CachyOS with Hyprland and Quickshell, Python 3, base-devel, CMake, Ninja,
pkgconf, Qt 6 (base, declarative, Wayland, SVG, multimedia and 5compat),
qtermwidget, Wayland headers/protocols and the current Hyprland development
headers. The generated PKGBUILD lists the complete runtime dependencies,
including Ghostty, Nautilus, LocalSend and the desktop helpers.

Do not copy native binaries from another installation. The plugins and terminal
module must be built against the actual Hyprland, Qt and qtermwidget versions
on the target machine. Installations made from the WinDoesNot packages receive
updates through the signed update channel; see
https://windoesnot.me/hilfe/paketupdates/ for the one-time setup.

Build the split desktop packages
-------------------------------
From the extracted directory, as your normal user:

    python3 tools/prepare-packages.py --output build/local-packages
    cd build/local-packages
    makepkg -s

Review the generated PKGBUILD and package dependencies. After making an
independent backup, the four locally built packages can be installed with:

    sudo pacman -U ./*.pkg.tar.zst

The packages supply the WinDoesNot login session and managed desktop code.
Choose the WinDoesNot session at login. The user initializer creates missing
defaults and preserves existing personal preferences; it does not replace a
system backup. Do not blindly overwrite ~/.config with desktop/config.

Contents and limitations
------------------------
- desktop/config: portable code; desktop/defaults: separate neutral defaults.
- desktop/plugins and vendor: sources for native modules, with original notices.
- packaging: dependency recipes, version, changelog and license notes.
- No host settings, private histories, credentials, backups or compiled plugins.
- The source package build path is used for the ISO. Installing this standalone
  source export on other systems has not been separately smoke-tested.
- Real hardware, BIOS boot and Secure Boot are not yet verified.

Project code is GPL-3.0-or-later. Third-party components retain their licenses;
read LICENSE, THIRD-PARTY.md and packaging/LICENSE-NOTES.md.
